2026-11-04T20:30:51.390284951Z          a password, even if POSTGRES_PASSWORD is set. See PostgreSQL
2026-11-04T20:30:51.390288679Z          documentation about "trust":
2026-11-04T20:30:51.390292524Z          https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/auth-trust.html
2026-11-04T20:30:51.390296094Z          In Docker's default configuration, this is effectively any other
2026-11-04T20:30:51.390299802Z          container on the same system.
2026-11-04T20:30:51.390303318Z 
2026-11-04T20:30:51.390306608Z          It is not recommended to use POSTGRES_HOST_AUTH_METHOD=trust. Replace
2026-11-04T20:30:51.390310131Z          it with "-e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=password" instead to set a password in
2026-11-04T20:30:51.390313941Z          "docker run".
